hape","kind":"rectangle","position":{"x":10720,"y":4770},"width":1720,"height":120,"fillColor":"#607d8b","text":"Facilitation guide","textFontFamily":"Inter","textAlignment":"left","attachedFrame":"Ms1_aPOGluwtqxJ_fLoIf","textSize":56,"textColor":"#ffffff","textBold":true},{"id":"HsfXW1ZdrhW51cy8kPOX3","type":"shape","kind":"rectangle","position":{"x":10740,"y":4940},"width":1680,"height":1060,"fillColor":"transparent","text":"🚀 SWOT Strategy: How it works in 4 steps\n\n🎯 Purpose: Derive concrete strategies from a SWOT analysis.\n\n1. Transfer the SWOT (10 min)\nAction: Place the top Strengths and Weaknesses in the \"Company\" rows and the top Chances and Risks in the \"Environment\" columns.\n\n2. Combine (30 min)\nAction: Work through the four fields:\nDEVELOP (strengths × chances): use strengths to seize chances.\nPROTECT (strengths × risks): use strengths to defend against risks.\nREGAIN (weaknesses × chances): use chances to overcome weaknesses.\nAVOID (weaknesses × risks): reduce exposure where both meet.\nRule: Each strategy card names the factors it combines.\n\n3. Prioritise (10 min)\nAction: Rate strategies by impact and effort, dot-vote the top 3.\n\n4. Plan (15 min)\nAction: Give each top strategy an owner and a first step.\n\n🛠️ Your role as facilitator\nConnector: Ask \"Which strength helps with this chance?\"\nRealist: Keep strategies concrete and testable.\nDecider: Close with clear owners.","textFontFamily":"Inter","textAlignment":"left","attachedFrame":"Ms1_aPOGluwtqxJ_fLoIf","textSize":26,"textColor":"#000000"}]}]}}